description "runs SSG's own remediation for the profile the image conforms to, leaving every rule a module claims or refuses alone"

supports "fedora"

// The capability is how `tect check` tells an image that declares `conforms`
// and installs nothing to act on it. Nothing requires it: an image measured
// without being remediated is a real thing to want.
provides "scap-remediation"

// No `satisfies`. The rules this closes are SSG's work, not this module's, and
// a claim here would say the module makes them pass when the content does.
